{
  "$comment": [
    "Core declarations. Read at boot; the binaries are NOT. Each entry is metadata",
    "the Rust registry stores as a CoreDescriptor so the UI can decide which core a",
    "game needs without loading anything.",
    "",
    "Every entry currently points at cores/diagnostic-core.wasm — a valid but empty",
    "module. Phase 1b replaces `module` per entry with the real libretro core built",
    "to wasm32, and drops the `placeholder` flag. Nothing else here changes: the",
    "geometry, refresh and audio values below are the real values for each system,",
    "and they are what the pacer and renderer are already configured from.",
    "",
    "`targetFps` values are the true hardware refresh rates, not rounded to 60. A",
    "core running at 60.0988 against a 60.000 display is why the frame pacer exists."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "cores": [
    {
      "id": "nestopia",
      "name": "Nestopia UE",
      "systems": ["nes"],
      "module": "./cores/diagnostic-core.wasm",
      "placeholder": true,
      "sizeBytes": 8,
      "targetFps": 60.0988,
      "audioSampleRate": 44100,
      "pixelFormat": "xrgb8888",
      "geometry": {
        "baseWidth": 256,
        "baseHeight": 240,
        "maxWidth": 256,
        "maxHeight": 240,
        "aspectRatio": 1.3333333
      }
    },
    {
